  "narrative": {
    "top_frame": "The eighth inning is where they live now. Down three with three innings left, they didn't fold. Campusano broke a 4-4 tie with a single that became four runs, and that one swing is why this team is 3-0 instead of looking at another loss. The game was fragile until it wasn't.",
    "what_this_means": "Campusano's at-bat mattered because the Padres had scraped together four hits and seven strikeouts through seven innings, which is not offense. It's survival. Mize gave them five and two-thirds solid innings on 3.70 ERA form, and the bullpen held. V\u00e1squez, Matsui, Morgan, and Morejon kept Washington quiet after the Nationals scored twice in the sixth to take the lead. That half-inning was the game's only real moment of collapse, and it looked like the story until Campusano arrived. The win came because the back end of the order didn't blink when it had to. Three straight one-run wins. That math gets harder.",
    "what_to_watch": "Washington starts Kent tonight at 1:10 PT, a 5.55 ERA arm the Padres should attack early. Buehler has a 2.86 ERA over his last four starts and the lineup needs to make that count.",
